# Commit and PR conventions

- Commit messages: `type(scope): summary` (feat, fix, chore, refactor, docs, test). Imperative mood, focused commits.
- Include the issue/ticket id in the commit and PR body when one exists.
- PR descriptions are validation-first: state what changed, why, and concrete "Verify that…" steps a reviewer (human or agent) can run. Keep steps environment-neutral.
- Include screenshots for user-facing UI changes; call out migrations, flags, and rollout/rollback notes.
